    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional, validated-when-present `postcode` (4 digits) to owners, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml`)** \u2014 added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional, `^[0-9]{4}$`), so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain `getPostcode()`/`setPostcode()`. Since `Owner` extends `OwnerFields`, it's returned automatically.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added a `postcode` column to the `Owner` entity (with accessors) and to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`). MapStruct maps it by name in both directions, no mapper change needed.\n\n**Validation logic** \u2014 split across single-responsibility units:\n- `model/RegionPostcodes` \u2014 the fixed region\u2192range table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) with `isInRange(region, postcode)`; an unknown region imposes no constraint. This composes with the existing `CityRegion` (city\u2192region) rather than duplicating that table.\n- `rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerPostcode` \u2014 an OfficeFloor step that skips blank postcodes, and otherwise rejects a non-4-digit or out-of-range value, mirroring the existing `NormalizeOwnerEmail` optional-field pattern.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`, matching the existing `InvalidEmailException` handler shape.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 inserted `validatePostcode` into both the `POST /api/owners` pipeline (after required-field validation) and the `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline (after `ValidateOwner`), and added `owner.setPostcode(...)` to `ApplyOwner` so updates persist it.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 3/3 pass (valid postcode stored & returned, owner without postcode accepted, malformed postcode \u2192 400); `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
